  "amendment_date": "2026-10-21",
  "amendment": "Preserve current main behavior (98e64a6 at this merge), including independent per-key completions, immediate CEC admission while ACKs are pending, wait_for_release and fixed Siri macros. Distribution only moves messages to their owner and has zero CEC behavioral effect; d50af8026938797fc0820d0107f4c4e064c2d2bc remains historical evidence where unchanged. State-change-only transport; executor owns button/message choices and successful completion pacing, has no TX buffer and supplies one attempt per key press. Failed key TX ends that key state; later up is a no-op. Global release is implicit at recipient stream end only when all its keys cease being pressed, including last-key failure. CEC mechanically sends supplied frames through eight normal slots plus one release-only overflow slot per wire; releases at nine are dropped without executor admission retry. Necessary bounded task communication queues remain permitted, not outgoing/retry backlogs. Prior original-controller/headless, baseline-UI, hostname, settings, removal-reset and manual-recovery amendments remain in force.",
  "source_repository": "https://github.com/retsyx/amity-esp32",
  "source_commit": "d50af8026938797fc0820d0107f4c4e064c2d2bc",
  "status": "Current design package; software and physical validation are recorded separately in IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.json.",
